FACTS p390r-whatsnew {"errors":[],"facts":{"entry":"Club Manager: (P) and (O.G) beside a goal, and Quick Sim uses the bench. You asked for all three. In Club Manager a penalty now reads (P) after the scorer everywhere a goal is listed: the full time report, the match timeline and the live match. And now and then a goal is an own goal, marked (O.G) under the club that got it, with the defender or keeper who put it into his own net. It is always one of the goals the match already had, so no score, result or table moves. The player who would have had it loses it from his season, nobody else gains it, and an own goal has no assist. A penalty is never an own goal, and a shootout kick is not a goal, so it gets no mark. And when you Quick Sim, the coach now makes changes after the break too, not only for injuries: around the hour and again in the run in he takes off a booked man or the most tired legs for a fresher player who plays there, as long as the side is no weaker for it, or whatever it costs once you are two goals clear. He keeps one change back for an injury, and the full time report lists every sub he made."}}
